 & mean & std.\\ error of the mean & standard deviation \$\\sigma\$ & min & max \\\\\\midrule
\$C_D\$ & \\num{$CD} & \\num{$CDSE} & \\num{$CDSD} & \\num{$CDMIN} & \\num{$CDMAX} \\\\
\$C_L\$ & \\num{$CL} & \\num{$CLSE} & \\num{$CLSD} & \\num{$CLMIN} & \\num{$CLMAX} \\\\
\$C_{L,\\mathrm{front}}\$, \$C_{L,\\mathrm{rear}}\$ & \\num{$CLF}, \\num{$CLR} & & & & \\\\
\$C_M\$ & \\num{$CM} & & & & \\\\\\bottomrule
\\end{tabular}
\\caption{Aerodynamic coefficients over the stable part of the history, from iteration $FROM to $NIT ($WIN iterations; start found with the MSER rule, see the section Convergence); standard error of the mean with 10 batch means (the uncertainty of the mean due to the finite number of iterations); variance = \$\\sigma^2\$
(\$A_\\mathrm{ref}\$ = ${refArea:-frontal} area, \\SI{$refAreaValue}{m^2}; \$l_\\mathrm{ref}\$ = chord of the wing elements, \\SI{$refLength}{m}; lift along \$+z\$: downforce gives \$C_L<0\$).}
\\end{table}
$([ -n "$CdReference" ] && echo "\noindent Experimental \$C_D\$: \num{$CdReference}; difference \SI{$CDERR}{\percent}.")
$([ -n "$EXPROW" ] && cat <<VAL

\\section{Comparison with the experiment}
\\begin{table}[H]\\centering
\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\\toprule
 & experiment & CFD & difference \\\\\\midrule
