\$C_D\$ & \\num{$EXPCD} & \\num{$CD} & \\SI{$CDERRX}{\\percent} \\\\\\bottomrule
\\end{tabular}
\\caption{Tyrrell 026 single-element wing in freestream at the quoted incidence of \\SI{$ANGLE}{\\degree} (true \\SI{$(calc "$ANGLE + 2.45")}{\\degree}), k-\$\\omega\$ SST with \$a_1\$ = \\num{${A1:-0}}. Experiment: balance data of Zerihan (2001), chapter 3 (\\texttt{experiment.csv}, read from Figure 4 of the thesis, about \$\\pm 0.01\$ on \$C_L\$), free transition, \$Re \\approx 0.45 \\times 10^6\$; \$C_L = L/(q_\\infty c b)\$, \$C_D = D/(q_\\infty c b)\$. The CFD is fully turbulent.}
\\end{table}
$(fig wssx_bottom "Suction side seen from below: skin friction along the flow \$C_{f,x} = -\\tau_x/(0.5 U_\\infty^2)\$; red: attached flow, blue: reversed flow; the white line between them is the separation line.")
VAL
)
$([ -n "$FORCES" ] && cat <<FRC

\\section{Forces: drag, downforce and efficiency}
\\begin{table}[H]\\centering
\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\\toprule
 & simulated [N] & whole wing [N] & coefficient \\\\\\midrule
Drag \$D\$ & \\num{$FDf} & \\num{$FD2} & \$C_D\$ = \\num{$CD} \\\\
Downforce \$L = -F_z\$ & \\num{$(f2 $(calc "-1 * $FL"))} & \\num{$(f2 $(calc "-1 * $FACT * $FL"))} & \$C_L\$ = \\num{$CL} \\\\
Friction \$F_f\$ & \\num{$FDVf} & \\num{$FF2} & \$C_f\$ = \\num{$CFW} \\\\\\midrule
Efficiency \$E = L/D\$ & \\multicolumn{3}{c}{\\num{$EFF}} \\\\\\bottomrule
\\end{tabular}
\\caption{Forces on the walls (\\texttt{forces} function), mean over the same iterations as the coefficients (from $FROM to $NIT).
Friction: the wall shear stress integrated over the walls, along the flow; it is \\SI{$PDV}{\\percent} of the drag, the rest (\\SI{$PDP}{\\percent}, \\num{$FDPf} N) is pressure drag.
\$C_f = F_f / (0.5 \\rho_\\infty U_\\infty^2 S_\\mathrm{wet})\$, mean skin-friction coefficient over the wetted area (\$c_f\$ = \\num{$cf} assumed for the near-wall mesh).
$([ "$halfModel" = yes ] && echo "The simulation covers half of the wing (symmetry plane): whole wing = twice the simulated half." || echo "The simulation covers the whole wing.")
\$\\rho_\\infty\$ = \\SI{$rhoInf}{kg/m^3}, \$U_\\infty\$ = \\SI{$uInf}{m/s}.}
\\end{table}
FRC
)
$([ -n "$REGROWS" ] && cat <<REG
\\begin{table}[H]\\centering
\\begin{tabular}{lcc}\\toprule
Region & drag [N] & downforce [N] \\\\\\midrule
$REGROWS\\bottomrule
\\end{tabular}
\\caption{Forces of each part of the wing (one \\texttt{forces} function per region of the STL, \\texttt{system/regionForces}), pressure and viscous, mean over the same iterations; whole wing.}
\\end{table}
REG
)

\\section{Convergence}\\label{sec:convergence}
The averages use only the stable part of the history of \$C_D\$ and \$C_L\$. Its start is found with the MSER rule (Marginal Standard Error Rule): the first iteration \$d\$ that minimises \$\\sum_{i \\ge d} (y_i - \\bar y_d)^2 / (n - d)^2\$, that is the uncertainty of the mean of the iterations that are kept. For this run \$d = $FROM\$ ($FROMCD for \$C_D\$, $FROMCL for \$C_L\$; the later is used).$([ "$UNSTABLE" = 1 ] && echo " \\textbf{Warning:} the start falls at the end of the search range (half of the iterations): the history is still in its transient, more iterations are needed.")

$(fig residuals "Initial residuals of each equation (\\texttt{solverInfo}).")
$(fig inlet "Mean pressure coefficient on the inlet patch (\\texttt{inletPressure}), every iteration$([ -n "$CPIN" ] && echo "; last value \\num{$CPIN}"): it must settle to a constant, the blockage of the wing felt upstream.")
$(fig coeffs "History of \$C_D\$ and \$C_L\$ from iteration $(calc "int($NIT / 10)"); the first tenth, the start from the initial field, is left out. Dashed: means over the stable part (from iteration $FROM).")

\\section{Wall: \$y^+\$}
$([ -n "$YPROWS" ] && cat <<YPT
